  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "A sequence of numbers starts with \\(1,\\) \\(2,\\) and \\(3.\\) The fourth number of the sequence is the sum of the previous three numbers in the sequence: \\(1 + 2 + 3 = 6.\\) In the same way, every number after the fourth is the sum of the previous three numbers. What is the eighth number in the sequence?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(11\\)",
    "B": "\\(20\\)",
    "C": "\\(37\\)",
    "D": "\\(68\\)",
    "E": "\\(99\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each new number uses the three immediately preceding numbers, so calculate the terms in order. Starting with \\(1,2,3,6\\), we get\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{5th: }&2+3+6=11,\\\\\n\\text{6th: }&3+6+11=20,\\\\\n\\text{7th: }&6+11+20=37,\\\\\n\\text{8th: }&11+20+37=68.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe eighth number is \\(\\boxed{68}\\), choice D.",
